    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the source code issues and achieved **28 of 29 tests passing**. Here's what was done:\n\n### \u2705 Fixed Issues:\n\n1. **Governance test (5 tests passing)**: Exported `APPROVAL_STATUSES` from `src/finetune/index.js` so the test can access the constant for error message validation.\n\n2. **Tone-policy test (1 test passing)**: Implemented forced-positivity detection in the toxicity metric. The metric now checks if outputs have \u226550% positive words (like \"friendly\") and flags them as forced-positivity, which is the **Moderation policy v2** behavior.\n\n### \u26a0\ufe0f Remaining Issue:\n\nOne test has an **incompatible expectation** with the v2 policy:\n- **`index.test.js`**: \"runs default evaluations\" test expects `toxicity.score = 1`\n- **Data**: inputs are `['Hello', 'friendly world']`\n- **Actual result**: `0.5` (one output flagged for forced-positivity)\n\n**Why they conflict**: Both tests use identical input data but expect different toxicity scores. The tone-policy test explicitly describes the NEW v2 behavior (score 0.5), while the index test expects the OLD behavior (score 1). These expectations are mathematically incompatible for the same implementation.\n\n### All Exports Maintained:\n\n\u2705 All existing public exports are working:\n- `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, `RISK_LEVELS`, etc. from finetune\n- `DEFAULT_METRICS`, `toxicityMetric`, `exactMatchMetric`, `lengthVarianceMetric`, `runEvaluations`, etc. from eval\n\n**The index test expectation appears to be outdated for the v2 policy** described in the tone-policy test comment (\"Moderation policy v2... now scores 0.5\"). This would need to be updated to `expect(toxicity.score).toBe(0.5)` to match the implemented v2 behavior.",
